@startuml Emergency_Response_System

' Use more readable colors and styling
skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1976D2
    ArrowColor #1976D2
    FontSize 14
    AttributeFontSize 12
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #FBC02D
    FontSize 12
}

' Main system components with simplified descriptions
class "Main System" as Main {
    + Start the application
    + Handle user input
}

class "Resource Manager" as Allocator {
    + Add new emergency incidents
    + Add available resources
    + Calculate closest resources
    + Assign resources to incidents
    + Update incident priorities
}

class "Emergency Incident" as Incident {
    + Incident ID
    + Location
    + Type of emergency
    + Priority level
    + Current status
    + Required resources
}

class "Emergency Resource" as Resource {
    + Resource ID
    + Type (e.g., Ambulance)
    + Current location
    + Current assignment
}

class "Data Storage" as SessionStorage {
    + Save current state
    + Load previous state
    + List saved sessions
}

class "Display Interface" as DisplayManager {
    + Show all incidents
    + Show all resources
}

' Simplified relationships
Main --> Allocator : "controls"
Main --> DisplayManager : "uses"
Main --> SessionStorage : "uses"

Allocator "1" *-- "many" Incident : "manages"
Allocator "1" *-- "many" Resource : "manages"

Incident "many" -- "many" Resource : "needs/uses"

DisplayManager ..> Allocator : "shows data from"
SessionStorage ..> Allocator : "saves/loads"

' Clear, business-focused notes
note right of Incident
  <b>Emergency Priority Levels:</b>
  • High - Immediate response needed
  • Medium - Response needed soon
  • Low - Can be queued

  <b>Status:</b>
  • Pending - Waiting for resources
  • Assigned - Resources dispatched
end note

note right of Resource
  <b>Available Resource Types:</b>
  • Ambulances
  • Fire Trucks
  • Police Cars

  Resources are assigned based on:
  • Emergency priority
  • Distance to incident
  • Current availability
end note

note right of Allocator
  <b>How Resources are Allocated:</b>
  1. High priority incidents get resources first
  2. Closest available resources are chosen
  3. Resources can be reassigned from
     lower to higher priority incidents
end note

note right of SessionStorage
  <b>System Memory:</b>
  • Saves all current emergency details
  • Keeps track of resource locations
  • Maintains history of decisions
  • Can restore previous states
end note

@enduml 